content.thinking:
The raw brickHit works correctly! So the problem is in my TEST — the `isolate` helper. Let me look:

```js
function isolate(bricks, ...keep) {
  for (const b of bricks) {
    if (!keep.includes(b)) b.alive = false;
  }
  return bricks;
}
```

And in the test:
```js
const brick = brickAt(makeBricks(1), 244, 104);
const bricks = isolate(makeBricks(1), brick);
```

`brick` comes from a DIFFERENT makeBricks(1) call than `bricks`! The objects are not the same references, so `keep.includes(b)` is false for all bricks in the second grid → ALL dead → no hit!

That's the bug in my test. Fix: use the same grid:

```js
const bricks = makeBricks(1);
const brick = brickAt(bricks, 244, 104);
const bricks2 = isolate(bricks, brick);
```

